Fundamental interpretation: The Prime Atlas is a discrete arithmetic dynamical system in which prime factors generate modular exclusion constraints. Wheel geometry describes the surviving integers, phase functions encode divisibility, and collective interference encodes relationships among modular states.

The next formal stage is to derive phase-correlation evolution equations connecting wheel gaps, modular intersections, and higher-order interference. These could reveal structure beyond the individual resonance conditions without presupposing a computational breakthrough.
